{
 "about": "Polls as katzenqt's tally code keeps them: one Yjs document a survey, its root map meta {survey_id (hex), topic, mode, n_slots, status open or closed, creator (hex voter id)}, root array slots of maps {id, text}, root map votes of voter id (hex) to a map of slot id to availability with _version. A member's voter id is BLAKE2b-128 of its key. A create or sync response carries an update, merged in; a vote carries the sender's choice, recorded under the sender's voter id when its slots are the survey's and its availabilities the mode's (approval: yes, no; availability: yes, maybe, no), the newest version winning and an equal one replacing; a close counts from the survey's creator only; a sync request is answered with the diff since its state vector. A vote or close for a survey not yet seen waits for it. Survey ids over 64 bytes and updates over 512 KiB are refused (the second is not among the vectors, for size). Counts take a slot not marked as no; the winners are the slots with the most yes, none when no slot has one. Generated by scripts/gen_tally_poll_scenarios.py with katzenqt's tally code.",
